WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.402
Hi! How do scientists sort millions of living things? They classify them by their features. Today we'll learn to classify living things with a chart.

2
00:00:12.552 --> 00:00:18.114
Living things can be grouped into plants, animals, fungi and bacteria.

3
00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:21.378
Plants are green and make their own food.

4
00:00:21.528 --> 00:00:25.794
Animals eat plants or other animals, and many move about.

5
00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:33.378
Fungi reproduce by spores. Bacteria are so tiny we need a microscope.

6
00:00:33.528 --> 00:00:40.962
Each step of a chart asks one question. The answer, yes or no, splits the living things into two groups.

7
00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:47.058
For example: does it flower? Hibiscus goes under yes, and fern under no.

8
00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:53.298
Then ask: does it have 6 legs? Ant goes under yes, and spider under no.

9
00:00:53.448 --> 00:01:00.378
A good sorting question uses features we can observe or measure, not "Is it pretty?"

10
00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:06.474
Watch out! Some pupils sort by asking "Is it cute?" That doesn't work!

11
00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:11.370
People have different ideas about what's cute, so they'd sort differently.

12
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:18.282
Use features everyone can see, like: does it have feathers? Does it flower?

13
00:01:18.432 --> 00:01:27.186
Your turn! Which big group does a mushroom belong to? Pause and think.

14
00:01:27.336 --> 00:01:32.586
A mushroom is a fungus. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:32.736 --> 00:01:42.978
Another one! For the question "Does it flower?", which group does a fern go in? Pause and think.

16
00:01:43.128 --> 00:01:49.362
Ferns don't flower, so it goes in the no group. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:49.512 --> 00:01:59.610
Here's another! For "Does it have 6 legs?", which group does a spider go in? Pause and think.

18
00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:06.330
A spider has 8 legs, so it goes in the no group. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:17.394
Try one more! Which is a better sorting question: "Does it have wings?" or "Does it look nice?" Pause and think.

20
00:02:17.544 --> 00:02:24.450
Everyone can see whether it has wings, so that's a good question. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:34.050
Try one more! Which big group of living things makes its own food? Pause and think.

22
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.306
Plants make their own food. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:39.456 --> 00:02:49.890
Last one! Mushrooms and bread mould go in the same group. What are they both? Pause and think.

24
00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:57.018
They are both fungi. Neither can make its own food. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:57.168 --> 00:03:08.346
Remember: living things can be grouped into plants, animals, fungi and bacteria. A chart asks one question at each step, using features we can observe.

26
00:03:08.496 --> 00:03:13.074
Try classifying your toy animals at home!

